# PART 4 — A–D PAPER VERSION GENERATION

After the COE selects and confirms a numbered question set for an examination sitting, the backend generates four shuffled versions:

- Version A.
- Version B.
- Version C.
- Version D.

Each version contains the same questions from the selected numbered set.

Only the following are shuffled:
- Question order.
- Answer-option order.

Stable Question IDs must remain unchanged across versions.

The correct answer mapping must be transformed correctly when options are shuffled.

The backend must generate and preserve:
- Version A question ordering and option ordering.
- Version B question ordering and option ordering.
- Version C question ordering and option ordering.
- Version D question ordering and option ordering.
- Stable Question ID mapping.
- Correct answer mapping for evaluation.

These are four versions of ONE selected numbered set, not four separate numbered sets.

Do not allow A–D version generation to use different question pools.

Preserve the relationship between:
- Examination ID.
- Sitting ID.
- Selected numbered set ID.
- Question-bank revision ID.
- Blueprint revision ID.
- A–D version IDs.

