# PART 8 — TWO COMPLETELY SEPARATE CREDENTIAL SYSTEMS

This is the most important new security requirement.

The system must maintain two independent credentials for two different purposes.

## SYSTEM A — PERMANENT LAB-SPECIFIC PC RECOVERY CREDENTIAL

Purpose: Allow the authorised Lab Administrator or Lab Instructor to open the recovery console and authorise a student to resume an interrupted examination on another PC after a workstation crash or failure.

### Credential model

Each physical computer laboratory has its own Lab Administrator account.

For example:

| Laboratory | Username | Credential scope |
|---|---|---|
| Lab 1 | labadmin01 | Lab 1 only |
| Lab 2 | labadmin02 | Lab 2 only |
| Lab 3 | labadmin03 | Lab 3 only |

These usernames and passwords are configured once through the authorised institutional account provisioning process.

They remain the same across different examination sessions until an authorised administrator changes or rotates them.

### Important rules

1. Every laboratory must have a distinct account.
2. Do not use one institution-wide shared recovery password.
3. Do not generate a new Lab Administrator password for every examination.
4. Do not automatically change the lab credential at the end of an examination.
5. Do not generate these permanent lab credentials from the COE session unlock feature.
6. Do not expose stored passwords in the COE Portal.
7. Store only secure password hashes in the backend or Lab Server credential store.
8. Credentials must be revocable and changeable by an authorised institutional administrator.
9. Do not hardcode usernames or passwords in React source code.
10. Lab Administrator permissions must be limited to the assigned laboratory.

The permanent Lab Administrator credentials must be available to the Lab Server while the student examination is offline.

The Lab Server must authenticate the Lab Administrator locally or through the authorised college LAN service. The recovery feature must not depend on an active Internet connection.

The COE Portal may display laboratory identity and recovery configuration status, but it must not reveal the permanent passwords.

### Where this login appears

The Student Portal will have a separate option:

**Lab Administrator / Recovery Login**

This must be different from student login.

The lab instructor authenticates using their assigned laboratory account and opens the authorised recovery console.

The actual Student Portal login-page implementation is maintained in the separate Student Portal project. Do not merge that application into the COE project.

Prepare the necessary authentication API contract and integration requirements.

