# PART 10 — PC CRASH RECOVERY WORKFLOW

The Lab Administrator credential and recovery workflow must be separate from the session unlock credential.

### Scenario

A student is writing an examination and their PC crashes.

The student needs to continue using another available computer.

### Recovery workflow

1. Student's current PC crashes or loses its active connection.
2. Lab Server detects the interrupted connection or heartbeat timeout.
3. Student is marked Interrupted / Recovery Required after the configured detection policy.
4. Lab Administrator opens the Student Portal recovery login.
5. Lab Administrator enters the permanent credentials for that specific laboratory.
6. Lab Server authenticates the account and identifies its authorised laboratory.
7. Lab Administrator opens the recovery console.
8. Search for the affected student using USN.
9. Display the student's:
   - Name.
   - USN.
   - Examination.
   - Sitting.
   - Original Section.
   - Current session status.
   - Last active PC.
   - Last saved response timestamp.
10. Lab Administrator selects the affected student and initiates recovery.
11. Require a reason for the recovery.
12. Select an available replacement PC in the authorised recovery scope.
13. Lab Server revokes the old workstation binding.
14. Lab Server creates a secure single-use, expiring recovery authorisation bound to the student, examination, sitting and new PC.
15. Student logs in on the new PC.
16. Lab Server verifies the recovery authorisation.
17. Lab Server restores the server-confirmed saved answers and remaining timer.
18. Student continues the same examination.

### Preserve these values without changing them

- Student ID.
- USN.
- Examination ID.
- Sitting ID.
- Selected numbered set ID.
- Assigned A/B/C/D paper version.
- Stable Question ID mapping.
- Saved responses.
- Remaining examination time.
- Submission status and session history.

Moving computers must NEVER regenerate the paper version or create a new examination attempt.

### One active workstation rule

A student may have only one active workstation at any time.

On successful recovery:
- Revoke the old PC token/session.
- Allow the new PC to become the only active workstation.
- Reject future requests from the old workstation.
- Prevent two PCs from concurrently writing answers for the same student.

### Lab scope

The permanent Lab Administrator account must be restricted to its own laboratory.

If the student needs to move to another laboratory, require an authorised cross-lab recovery process rather than allowing any Lab Administrator to access any laboratory.

### Recovery audit

Record:

- Student USN and internal Student ID.
- Examination ID.
- Sitting ID.
- Lab Administrator account.
- Original PC ID.
- Replacement PC ID.
- Recovery reason.
- Recovery timestamp.
- Recovery authorisation ID.
- Recovery status.

Do not log credentials, plaintext passwords, session unlock codes or sensitive authentication tokens.

