Keep them separate from production operations.

### Development mode

May support:
- Synthetic students.
- Synthetic workstation IDs.
- Demo examinations.
- Simulated Lab Server responses.
- Test session unlock credentials.
- Demo recovery events.
- Mock package verification.

Clearly label simulated functionality.

Never use real institutional credentials or real student information in demo data.

### Production mode

Must use:
- Real Java backend authentication.
- Real session credentials.
- Secure password storage.
- Secure signed package transfer.
- Real Lab Server verification.
- Real student version allocation.
- Real workstation binding and recovery.
- Protected audit records.

Never silently fall back to mock data when a production operation fails.

Never hardcode permanent lab passwords or session unlock credentials in frontend code.

Never claim successful Lab Server synchronization unless the Lab Server acknowledges it.

