# PART 19 — MANDATORY TEST SCENARIOS

### Test 1: USN-based version assignment

Use 60 synthetic students.

Expected:
- 15 students per version where the distribution is balanced.
- Version assignments randomised.
- No PC number influences the version.
- Assignments persist after refresh and logout/relogin.

### Test 2: Student changes PC

Student 4MH24CS001 is assigned Version C.

Initially logs in from PC-01.

After a simulated crash, authorised recovery moves the student to PC-15.

Expected:
- Version remains C.
- Same examination and sitting.
- Same saved answers.
- Same remaining time.
- Old PC binding revoked.
- PC-15 becomes Current PC.
- No duplicate active session.

### Test 3: Lab-specific recovery credential

Use two laboratory accounts.

Expected:
- Lab 1 credentials work only in Lab 1.
- Lab 2 credentials work only in Lab 2.
- Credentials remain unchanged across different examinations until authorised rotation.
- Lab credentials do not authorise session tab-switch unlocking by themselves.
- Account activity is logged.

### Test 4: Session unlock credential

Create two examination sittings.

Expected:
- Each sitting receives a different credential.
- Morning credential cannot unlock afternoon sitting.
- Credential works only within the authorised sitting period.
- Multiple legitimate unlocks can occur during the same active sitting.
- Every unlock is logged.
- Expired or revoked credentials are rejected.

### Test 5: Offline operation

Disconnect Internet access from the student laboratory environment.

Expected:
- Student login works through the college LAN and Lab Server.
- USN-based version retrieval works.
- Session unlock credential is verified locally.
- Lab Administrator recovery login works locally.
- Student recovery works without Internet access.

### Test 6: Dynamic numbered sets

Test an examination with one, two, three and more than four published numbered sets.

Expected:
- COE sees the exact number of available published sets.
- No fixed-four assumptions.
- Only published valid sets are selectable.
- Each sitting requires explicit set selection.

### Test 7: Security and audit

Verify:
- No passwords in frontend source code.
- No plaintext credentials in packages or audit logs.
- No cross-lab recovery.
- No cross-sitting session unlock.
- No duplicate active student workstation sessions.
- No version change during workstation recovery.
- No student-to-version mapping exposed to HOD.

