# PART 20 — FINAL EXPECTED RESULT

The COE Portal must follow these final institutional rules:

1. Numbered question-set availability is dynamic.
2. COE explicitly selects a published numbered set for each sitting.
3. A–D paper versions are generated from that selected numbered set.
4. Student paper versions are allocated by USN/student identity.
5. Paper version allocation never depends on PC numbers.
6. Students are not assigned PCs in advance.
7. Workstation association happens dynamically after successful login.
8. A student can recover on another PC without changing the paper version, answers or timer.
9. Each physical laboratory has its own permanent Lab Administrator recovery credentials.
10. Lab Administrator credentials remain the same across examinations until authorised rotation.
11. COE generates a separate session-specific unlock credential for each examination sitting.
12. The session unlock credential is used for authorised suspicious-activity/tab-switch screen unlocks.
13. The two credential systems are independent.
14. Lab Server supports these mechanisms locally without student Internet dependency.
15. Every recovery, unlock, version allocation and credential action is auditable.

